{
 "product_id": "p-fpd-001",
 "items": [
  {
   "key": "must:mh_trackers",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "The tracking set fitness buyers search for: a workout log, a weekly meal planner with a grocery list, a weight chart, a body measurements table and a weekly habit tracker."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_journal",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "Journal space, not only grids: Win of the week and Next week I will on every week page, How it felt and Next time on every workout, a monthly reflection, and three dot-grid notes pages."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_apps",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "One PDF that works in Goodnotes (named first in the title and listing), Notability, Samsung Notes, Xodo and Noteshelf on iPad, Android and Windows tablets."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_nav",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "Fully hyperlinked: Contents, month tabs on every page, a top bar (Home, Weeks, Workouts, Progress), previous and next arrows, and a trail back on every page."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_look",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "A finished, designed look with real typography and consistent spacing; design is the biggest praise driver."
  },
  {
   "key": "must:mh_guide",
   "kind": "must_have",
   "text": "Instructions printed inside the file (Start here and Setup check pages), not only in a separate PDF or video."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_not_useful",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_not_useful: Every page has a job a buyer does every week: plan the week, log the workout, plan the meals, tick what got done. Writing rows are at least 26 px tall and the workout table has 8 exercises by 4 sets. Photos show pages close up at real size so buyers can judge the space before buying, and the listing lists every page type with its count."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_download",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_download: Ships as one PDF, not a zip, with no sticker files that can fail to import. Listing copy and the apps photo give the download in 3 steps: buy, download from Etsy in a web browser (the Etsy app cannot download digital files), open the PDF in a note app. Start here repeats the steps. The cover title matches the listing name."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_misleading",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_misleading: Every listing photo is the built file, captioned with the page name; nothing is shown that the file lacks. The description says plainly: digital PDF for note apps on tablets, portrait, undated, English, no stickers, handwrite or use the app's text tool."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_value",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_value: Nothing to duplicate: 52 week pages, 52 meal plans and 208 workout logs are already in the file, all hyperlinked, so a buyer never copies pages to make more weeks (the exact 1-star complaint). The listing gives exact counts per page type from the built file."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_print",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_print: Made for tablets, and printable too: every page is 8 x 10.7 inches, smaller than both US Letter and A4, so a page prints at Actual size without cropping. Each week's pages sit together in the file (the week, its meal plan, its 4 workouts: 6 pages in a row), so one week prints as a single page range. The listing says how, and that the light page tint prints too."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_hard",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_hard: One starting point: the week page. It opens that week's meal plan and Workout 1 to 4 with buttons, and every one of those has a Week button back. Start here step 3 walks through exactly this. Habit circles sit in a plain 7-day grid with one habit per row and day names over every column, not a circle wheel."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_quality",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_quality: Every printed word on every page type is spell-checked before publishing, and the build checks 0 broken links, no unreachable pages and no overflowing text. All text is vector so it stays crisp at any zoom. Weeks, workouts and meal plans run in number order, each exactly once."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_basic",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_basic: Tools that make a plan work, not blank boxes: a Last time column on every exercise so each workout can beat the one before, a 52-week weight chart that shows the trend on one page, measuring every 4 weeks with a How to measure guide, and a meal grid with a tick for each meal eaten as planned."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_device",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_device: Portrait pages at the tablet's own upright shape, and every link is a plain PDF link that all major note apps follow. The listing has a Works with and Not for box: Goodnotes, Notability, Samsung Notes, Xodo and Noteshelf on iPad, Android and Windows tablets; not for phones, not Canva, not a spreadsheet, not a fillable form. The Setup check page proves it on the buyer's own device in one minute."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_missing",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_missing: No promised extras that can go missing: no stickers or bonus files are advertised, and the listing counts each page type from the built file (style rule r003). The 3-star complaint about no pages for tracking what you eat is answered by a meal plan for every week with a tick per meal and a grocery list."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_support",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_support: Most messages are 'it does not work' questions, so the answers are in the file and the listing: the Setup check fix list, the Start here steps and a listing FAQ with the top problems (Etsy app download, which app, links not tapping, how to type, printing). Reply speed is shop-level, and the file promises no reply times (style rule r007)."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_repetitive",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_repetitive: Each page type has one clear job and a different layout (week hub, workout log, meal plan, month check-in, chart, measurements). Repeats are the logs a buyer fills over a year, counted honestly in the listing as 52 weeks, 208 workout logs and 52 meal plans, never padded into a bigger page count."
  },
  {
   "key": "fix:f_broken",
   "kind": "fix",
   "text": "complaint:c_broken: The Setup check page: tap three buttons, and if one does not jump, a four-item fix list is right there (pen off, open in a note app, re-import as PDF, then message the shop)."
  },
  {
   "key": "unique:u_week_hub",
   "kind": "unique",
   "text": "One week, one tap: Each of the 52 week pages has buttons to that week's meal plan and Workout 1 to 4, and each of those pages has a Week button back. A 52-week overview opens any week, and the training log lists every workout by week with a button to each."
  },
  {
   "key": "unique:u_overload",
   "kind": "unique",
   "text": "Workout logs that help you get stronger: Every workout page has a Last time column next to each exercise: copy your best set from last time, then beat it, with weight x reps for 4 sets, an effort rating, a cardio table and Next time notes."
  },
  {
   "key": "unique:u_progress",
   "kind": "unique",
   "text": "A year of progress on one page: A 52-week weight chart (write your own scale, one dot a week), start and goal lines, milestones and wins the scale does not show, plus a measurements table every 4 weeks with a How to measure guide. Week 4, 8, 12 and so on show a Measure button."
  },
  {
   "key": "unique:u_start",
   "kind": "unique",
   "text": "Five-minute start and setup check: The cover's Open planner button lands on Start here: 4 numbered steps with Go there buttons. Setup check is next: buttons that jump and come back, with a fix list if they do not."
  },
  {
   "key": "unique:u_anytime",
   "kind": "unique",
   "text": "Start any day: Undated weeks and months: write the dates on Week 1 the day you start, whether that is a Tuesday in October or the first of June. Nothing is wasted if you start late in the year."
  },
  {
   "key": "look",
   "kind": "look",
   "text": "Athletic editorial, not pink, rose gold or kawaii, and not neon gym black. Cool off-white paper (#F8F7F3, softer than white in a dark room) with deep navy ink at about 15:1 contrast, so it stays sharp in daylight; muted text stays above 5:1. One cobalt accent for buttons and the chart, with a lime detail on the cover and as the end of the month-tab range (periwinkle to lime). Two fonts only: Libre Baskerville bold for headings and Baskerville italic for field labels; Outfit for body text, with semibold for buttons, days and tabs. No letter-spaced all-caps labels. Plain ruled decoration, no clip-art dumbbells or fruit."
  }
 ],
